  "content": {
    "id": "p16-q3-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "3",
    "prompt": "Factorise each of the following expressions:",
    "layout": "grid",
    "columns": 2,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p16-q3-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "$x^4-5x^2+4$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$(x-1)(x+1)(x-2)(x+2)$\n\nSubstitute for $x^2$, then use differences of squares.",
          "worked": "Let $u=x^2$. The numbers are $-1$ and $-4$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}x^4-5x^2+4&=u^2-5u+4\\\\x^4-5x^2+4&=(u-1)(u-4)\\\\x^4-5x^2+4&=(x^2-1)(x^2-4)\\\\x^4-5x^2+4&=(x-1)(x+1)(x-2)(x+2).\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 44
      },
      {
        "id": "p16-q3-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "$x^4-20x^2+64$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$(x-2)(x+2)(x-4)(x+4)$\n\nSubstitute for $x^2$, then use differences of squares.",
          "worked": "Let $u=x^2$. The numbers are $-4$ and $-16$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}x^4-20x^2+64&=u^2-20u+64\\\\x^4-20x^2+64&=(u-4)(u-16)\\\\x^4-20x^2+64&=(x^2-4)(x^2-16)\\\\x^4-20x^2+64&=(x-2)(x+2)(x-4)(x+4).\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 52
      },
      {
        "id": "p16-q3-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "$x^4-29x^2+100$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$(x-5)(x+5)(x-2)(x+2)$\n\nSubstitute for $x^2$, then use differences of squares.",
          "worked": "Let $u=x^2$. The numbers are $-25$ and $-4$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}x^4-29x^2+100&=u^2-29u+100\\\\x^4-29x^2+100&=(u-25)(u-4)\\\\x^4-29x^2+100&=(x^2-25)(x^2-4)\\\\x^4-29x^2+100&=(x-5)(x+5)(x-2)(x+2).\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 52
      },
      {
        "id": "p16-q3-d",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "d",
        "prompt": "$x^4-10x^2+9$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$(x-1)(x+1)(x-3)(x+3)$\n\nSubstitute for $x^2$, then use differences of squares.",
          "worked": "Let $u=x^2$. The numbers are $-1$ and $-9$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}x^4-10x^2+9&=u^2-10u+9\\\\x^4-10x^2+9&=(u-1)(u-9)\\\\x^4-10x^2+9&=(x^2-1)(x^2-9)\\\\x^4-10x^2+9&=(x-1)(x+1)(x-3)(x+3).\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 44
      }
    ]
  },
